==========================================
WEATHER PREDICTION — FULL SETUP & RUN GUIDE
==========================================

This project predicts weather parameters such as temperature, humidity, and rainfall using Python, Flask, and Machine Learning models.
It provides a simple web interface to input weather data and view predictions in real-time.

------------------------------------------------------------
1. CLONE THE REPOSITORY
------------------------------------------------------------
Open terminal or PowerShell and run:
git clone https://github.com/22f3001741/Weather-Prediction-.git
cd Weather-Prediction-

------------------------------------------------------------
2. IF YOU ALREADY HAVE A LOCAL FOLDER
------------------------------------------------------------
If you created the project locally and want to connect it to this repository:
git init
git remote add origin https://github.com/22f3001741/Weather-Prediction-.git
git branch -M main

------------------------------------------------------------
3. CREATE A VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENT
------------------------------------------------------------
Create an isolated environment for dependencies:
python -m venv venv

------------------------------------------------------------
4. ACTIVATE THE VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENT
------------------------------------------------------------
For Windows:
venv\Scripts\activate

For macOS/Linux:
source venv/bin/activate

------------------------------------------------------------
5. CREATE .gitignore FILE
------------------------------------------------------------
Add the following lines into a file named .gitignore:
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.db
*.sqlite3
.DS_Store
.env
*.log

Or create from PowerShell:
echo "venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.db
*.sqlite3
.DS_Store
.env
*.log" > .gitignore

------------------------------------------------------------
6. INSTALL DEPENDENCIES
------------------------------------------------------------
If requirements.txt exists:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Or install manually:
pip install flask pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib plotly requests

------------------------------------------------------------
7. UPDATE WEATHER DATA AND RUN MODEL PREDICTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------
After activating the virtual environment, run these commands one by one:

python scripts_v2/update_weather_data.py
(This script updates or fetches the latest weather data.)

python smart_predictions.py
(This script uses the ML model to generate or refresh predictions.)

------------------------------------------------------------
8. RUN THE FLASK APPLICATION (LAUNCH THE SERVER)
------------------------------------------------------------
Finally, start the Flask web server:
python .\app\main.py

You should see output like:
 * Running on http://127.0.0.1:5000/ (Press CTRL+C to quit)

------------------------------------------------------------
9. OPEN THE WEB APP
------------------------------------------------------------
Open a browser and visit:
http://127.0.0.1:5000/

You will see the Weather Prediction interface with live data and predictions.

